navigator.platform on Kosmos (docs/w7.md W7c): the system and its
processor, as Linux's uname gives "Linux x86_64" and Haiku says "Haiku",
matching the user agent's "Kosmos x86_64". It was empty, which no browser
a person uses answers and which a site's robot check reads as one that is
not - Google's search answered every query with its robot check.

diff -ruN a/Source/WebCore/page/NavigatorBase.cpp b/Source/WebCore/page/NavigatorBase.cpp
--- a/Source/WebCore/page/NavigatorBase.cpp	2026-11-14 19:11:42.209095809 -0300
+++ b/Source/WebCore/page/NavigatorBase.cpp	2026-11-14 19:11:42.222451866 -0300
@@ -110,6 +110,10 @@
     return "Win32"_s;
 #elif OS(HAIKU)
     return "Haiku"_s;
+#elif PLATFORM(KOSMOS) && CPU(X86_64)
+    return "Kosmos x86_64"_s;
+#elif PLATFORM(KOSMOS) && CPU(ARM64)
+    return "Kosmos aarch64"_s;
 #else
     return ""_s;
 #endif
